<title>UK: O.E. Pub bullish on current yr after profits.</title>
<headline>O.E. Pub bullish on current yr after profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Old English Pub Company said its performance in the first six weeks of the current financial year had showed good growth with sales more than doubling over the year-ago period.</p>
<p>The firm said sales were up 103 percent and it forecast 1997/98 as an &quot;exciting&quot; year ahead.</p>
<p>The company's pre-tax profit for the year ended March 30, 1997 rose to 1.6 million stg from 0.5 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>Turnover rose 111 percent to 14.7 million stg. The firm's earning per share was up to 7.77 pence from 2.86p as it proposed a final dividend of 1.2p, higher than last year's 0.67p.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
